amendments.new_text_outline:
- Create notes/inbox.md for raw dumps.
- Move the 8 Nov 'world interaction notes' dump out of DESIGN_NOTES (to end) into the inbox verbatim, then log one disposition row per paragraph in the dispositions appendix, then the design-notes skill empties the inbox (A-78).
- Row dispositions: (1) WASD free movement, not click-to-move -> integrated, section 7;
- (2) interact by moving near and pressing Space, menus on WASD/Space/Escape -> integrated, section 8;
- (3) dialogue as single readable chunks advanced by Space -> integrated, section 10;
- (4) pause menu on Escape when nothing else is open -> integrated, section 8;
- (5) camera centred on the player, with world events able to capture it and hand it back -> integrated only in part (S5-11): the control-frame latch and single zoom-out land with the first locomotion change, the capture/return directive stack lands with dialogue and events;
- (6) a single 'further out zoom' -> the single yaw-neutral zoom-out scalar (S5-11).
- Rows 5 and 6 are the items that only ever appeared in the dump, so they must not be lost.

- Log rejected options so they are not re-proposed: R6 seasonal council with rooms as scenes (rejected-by-review);
- R9 CK3 numeric odds (rejected-by-review; qualitative odds in advisor speech instead);
- S1-R9 re-rolled advisors weaken the through-line (rejected-by-owner, P3);
- S1-13 no epoch-handoff payoff (rejected-by-review, already specified in the epoch-transition section);
- S1-12 tone is only flavour (rejected-by-review, folded into S1-R2);
- R5C2 global 'important' accent (rejected, breaks P4); a LAYA-class or JEV-class decision model in the simulation path (rejected, INV-A); general probabilistic-programming engines, learned nets and JEPA-style world models at runtime (rejected, INV-F).
- Keep the S1-R9 label for the re-rolled-advisor row; R9 is only the CK3 numeric-odds route (label collision fixed).

- Write the eight rules as a numbered spine R1..R8, each one paragraph with a status and an enforcing test or lint named (or 'to be written'): R1 one watch clock;
- R2 actor and cause on every effect;
- R3 thread structure (stages, one spine thread in crisis_fuse);
- R4 discovery has a referent and an observer;
- R5 emergency cardinality and fuse (fuse built later, A-07);
- R6 reject instead of throw;
- R7 resource ledger;
- R8 epoch-end reads both ledgers and the Observation table.
- The section states it is revisable (P5).
- The minimal fields the owner named for S1-R1 are carried by A-16.
- Config gets a pointer, not a copy.
- AGENTS gets a pointer in A-66.
- No AGENTS pointer here; A-66 adds the pointer after the text exists.
- Owner wording to preserve verbatim: Accepts the 8-rule rules spine, leaving room to modify.

- Define the seven primitives: watch clock;
- Act (ground-truth event in a bounded ring; effects carry an optional causeActId via an envelope);
- Observation (who learned what; merges Report, Trace, Belief); presence function;
- ThreadRuntime / ResourceLedger / EmergencyRuntime slices;
- LineBrief plus gate;
- TextSourcePort.
- Storage is bounded (Tier 3 holds nothing, Tier 2 on demand, epoch end compacts into scars).
- Marked planned and revisable.
- Only DESIGN_NOTES carries it; section AGENTS/README pairs add each primitive in the change that ships it.
- Owner wording to preserve verbatim: Accepts the 7-primitive core model and the corrected order in slices/02b-roadmap-reorder.md, leaving plenty of room to add and modify.

- Authored/generated split: spine, Tier-1 bibles and keystones hand-authored with help;
- Tier-2, letters, gazette and rumours pool-generated and curated;
- Tier-3 templated.
- Authoring kit: CharacterBible, RegisterCard, few-shot builder, draft/accept CLI.
- Owner is happy to get help with authoring (P2).

- Slices are frozen on write and shared on read;
- StateSliceKey gains an optional schema, version and migrate plus a plain-JSON guard;
- WorldStateCodec owns snapshotVersion, Zod load, migrations and epoch check; saves carry packId and version.
- Decision S4-10: one registry per epoch.
- Fingerprint reconciliation is parked with the epoch-transition change.

- Tick phase order is commands, watch, materialize, kinematics, cognition, commit, flush; move outcomes (Arrived, Blocked, Interrupted) as data with residualDt; the door-closes-mid-route dwell and retarget-from-last-waypoint are fixed; zero-speed moves are rejected; the frame try/catch re-arms rAF;
- PlaySession.status is per call.
- Section AGENTS update rides the shipping change.

- Act record {id, actorId, verb, objectRef, motiveTag, spaceId, watch, perceptibility} in a frozen bounded ring; effect envelope {effect, actorId?, causeActId?};
- BehaviorModule gets a commit returning WorldEffect[]; stateless counter-based roll(worldSeed, streamKey, counter) for randomness inside Acts.
- Stimulus dedupe is A-88.

- Discovery layers (noticed, assayed, attributed, theorized) become a decaying view derived per observer from the Observation table; set_discovery_layer survives as a shim;
- Regard.exposure is no longer the only record of who knows what.
- INV-B details live here, decided before the Observation schema freezes: collapse parents sharing an origin or channel, spoof as a negative term, an order-independence test, a parent cap (ruling 17).

- InputState/InputFrame: keyup, blur and visibilitychange handled; event.code for physical keys; held and pressed sets; data action table;
- Space edge-triggered, no auto-repeat; dev HUD neutralised so Space cannot re-click it.
- Follows A-38 and keeps its tense and tag.

- Create the uplift-review-gates skill and move the gate briefs there verbatim (3-subagent spec audit, 2-subagent per-subtask review, 6-subagent post-change review).
- The AGENTS.md section shrinks to a pointer to the skill plus the OpenSpec commands; the config Review Gates block becomes a pointer.
- Additions only, nothing removed from any gate: G1 end-to-end feature trace (run the real entry point, name the producer and consumer call sites);
- G2 security / trust-boundary axis inside the adversarial reviewers;
- G3 hot-path cost axis inside the performance reviewer;
- G4 failure-containment axis inside the adversarial reviewers;
- G5 defect ledger (A-83);
- G6 scenario-to-test traceability check.
- The 'never reduce review' owner rule holds.
- The optional smoke script is dropped (ruling 16).
- No-loss: diff the moved gate briefs against the old text.

- One docs-truth test replaces the existence-and-length check and lands LAST in process-gates-and-ledger so it starts green (after roadmap.yaml, the ledger and the AGENTS rewrite exist).
- It asserts, for root AGENTS.md only at first: (1) backticked identifiers and npm scripts resolve to code or package.json, and every *Blueprint named in root AGENTS.md exists unless tagged '(planned)';
- (2) README versions match package.json and .nvmrc;
- (3) change ids appear only in openspec/ and DESIGN_NOTES.md;
- (4) DESIGN_NOTES status markers resolve to roadmap.yaml ids;
- (5) word budgets (AGENTS target about 900 with ceiling 1050; config context under 1.5k);
- (6) the roadmap DAG is valid and ids resolve;
- (7) the defect ledger rule (an entry that names an archived change or a change absent from roadmap.yaml fails; this is the single home of that check);
- (8) engine numbers against code constants (the default 7-epoch arc).
- The section-AGENTS *Blueprint check is added later in pre-05b-pack-source-of-truth.
